  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a four-component uncertainty model (probability, plausibility, credibility, possibility) and demonstrates simulated improvements in three application scenarios: cybersecurity anomaly detection (ROC‑AUC 0.78 → 0.88, FPR 0.14 → 0.06), quantum reinforcement learning convergence (1100 → 900 iterations), and portfolio optimization (Sharpe ratio 0.026 → 0.03, drawdown −18% → −15%). However, all results come from classical simulations and conceptual frameworks without implemented gate-based quantum algorithms.",
